# rsync exclude patterns for ensure-template-sync.sh (`--exclude-from`).
#
# Everything NOT listed here is replaced from the template on every sync, and
# anything in the destination that the template does not have is DELETED
# (`rsync -a --delete`). Excluded paths are exempt from both: they are neither
# transferred nor deleted.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ONLY THING STANDING BETWEEN `--delete` AND THE PCS'S LIVE
# STATE. Since the root move (2026-09-08) the destination is
# /DATA/AppData/yundera, which is not just the template tree — it is also where
# Authelia's user database, Dex's sqlite store, the TLS certs and the admin
# gate's sessions live. Before the move those sat safely outside the synced
# directory. Now a missing line here is a data-loss bug, which is why
# ensure-template-sync.sh dry-runs the delete list and refuses to proceed if a
# protected path is in it.
#
# `+ ` lines are INCLUDES and must come before the exclude they carve out of.
# Note the `/auth/**` form: excluding `/auth/` itself would stop rsync
# descending into the directory at all, and the include below could never match.

# --- the template's own file inside a protected directory --------------------
# Rendered by ensure-authelia.sh into auth/configuration.yml; the template is
# the only thing in auth/ we own, and it must keep being updated.
+ /auth/configuration.yml.tmpl

# --- per-host state that predates the root move ------------------------------
.env
.pcs.env
.pcs.secret.env
.ynd.user.env
# The WHOLE log directory, not `log/*.log`. logrotate is configured with
# `dateext` (ensure-logrotate.sh), so yesterday's file is `yundera.log-2026-09-02`
# and the compressed ones end `.gz` — neither matches `*.log`. Before the root
# move that only meant every template sync quietly deleted the rotated logs,
# defeating the 7-day retention; after it, the delete guard sees a protected
# path in the delete list and refuses to sync at all. Seen on wisera, 2026-09-08.
/log/**
*.backup
migration-markers/

# Written to the stack root by the PCS-to-PCS migration's stop_source step
# (settings-center-app Migration/steps/stopSource.ts) to keep the source's cron
# down. A sync landing mid-migration used to delete it and silently re-arm the
# cron on a box that was being migrated away from.
.self-check-cron-disabled

# --- runtime state now living inside the synced directory --------------------
# Authelia: users_database.yml, db.sqlite, secrets/, oidc/, clients.d/. Losing
# it drops the PCS back to UNCLAIMED — the owner's only local credential.
/auth/**
# Dex: dex.db, the rendered config, and connectors.d/ (which nothing
# regenerates — see ensure-dex.sh).
/dex/
# The rendered Dex theme and the two template files the dex container
# bind-mounts as FILES. Docker recreates a missing bind source as a directory,
# which makes dex permanently unstartable.
/dex-frontend/
# mesh-router-agent's certs and Caddy's state.
/data/
# The admin app's /app/data and the AppShield gate's sessions.
/admin/
# mesh-router-perf's store.
/perf/
# The onboarding `completed` marker.
/onboarding/
# Deployment overrides for tools/onboarding.sh. Nothing in the template tree
# creates this directory, so `--delete` used to remove it on the first sync
# after a deployment wrote one — which is how every demo PCS silently lost its
# onboarding skip overnight and served the first-run interstitial for the rest
# of the day (2026-09-10). See pcs-onboarding.md "The onboarding hook"; before
# the root move the override sat outside the synced directory and this line was
# not needed.
/onboarding.d/
# Set while a box is provisioning; self-check.sh refuses to run while it exists.
.provisioning-in-progress
# The tile icon Maison renders this stack from, placed at the flip.
.icon.svg
# Provenance marker from the retired mirrors. Kept so that a box rolled back to
# a template that still runs one finds its own marker and reclaims the folder
# instead of refusing to touch it.
.casaos-mirror
